<task id="111" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>UAT-R2 — fix the inline AI BubbleMenu toolbar layout (orphaned divider + nested Toolbar + overflow)</title>
    <phase>9 UAT-Fix</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <estimated-hours>3</estimated-hours>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <dependencies>none</dependencies>
    <blocks>114</blocks>
    <tags>pcf,react,fluent-ui,compose,frontend,uat-remediation</tags>
    <rigor-hint reason="Modifies .tsx UI; FULL; render-level DoD">FULL</rigor-hint>
    <model-tier reason="Contained Fluent v9 layout fix in a single widget; sonnet">sonnet</model-tier>
    <parallel-group>W1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe reason="Edits only ComposeAiToolbar.tsx + ComposeEditor.tsx (the BubbleMenu). Disjoint from 110 (BFF) and 112 (ConversationPane/formatter). No file overlap with any Wave-1 sibling.">true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    UAT defect #3a: when the user highlights text in Compose, the inline AI popup toolbar renders with broken
    layout. Root cause: `ComposeAiToolbar` returns a Fragment whose FIRST child is a bare `&lt;ToolbarDivider /&gt;`
    followed by a SECOND `&lt;Toolbar&gt;`, and both are mounted as direct children of the BubbleMenu flex row
    (`styles.bubbleMenu`) alongside the formatting `&lt;Toolbar&gt;`. Fluent v9 `ToolbarDivider` derives its
    orientation/height/margins from Toolbar context via `useToolbarContext` — rendered outside any Toolbar it
    collapses/misaligns; two sibling Toolbars each apply their own padding; and with no `flexWrap`/`maxWidth` the
    text-labelled AI buttons overflow the popup width. Fix so the popup is ONE clean, aligned bar.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Frontend engineer fluent in TipTap BubbleMenu + Fluent UI v9 Toolbar/ToolbarButton/ToolbarDivider composition
    and `makeStyles` token-based styling (ADR-021). You correct a Toolbar-composition bug without changing the
    action set, dispatch behavior, or the disabled-until-registered gating.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The selection popup renders as a single aligned toolbar: formatting controls, a properly-contextualized
    divider, then the AI action buttons — no collapsed/misaligned divider, no double padding, no horizontal
    overflow (buttons wrap or the bar caps to a sensible max-width). Dispatch wiring (handleActionClick →
    composeActionBridge) and the disabled-until-bindingId gating are unchanged.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Files: `ComposeAiToolbar.tsx:482-485` (the Fragment `&lt;&gt;&lt;ToolbarDivider/&gt;&lt;Toolbar .../&gt;`),
      `:357-363` (`styles.toolbar` re-imposing display:flex/columnGap over the Fluent Toolbar), `:219-260` (the 5
      DEFAULT_ACTIONS, each shipping `bindingId:''` → disabled until `registerComposeAiToolbarAction`). Host:
      `ComposeEditor.tsx:461-470` (`styles.bubbleMenu`, a center-aligned plain flex row), `:849-885` (the
      formatting `&lt;Toolbar&gt;`), `:848` (BubbleMenu), `:892-899` (where `&lt;ComposeAiToolbar/&gt;` is mounted).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="fix-toolbar-composition" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeAiToolbar.tsx</file>
      <file purpose="host-bubblemenu-and-toolbar" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <notes>
      Preferred fix: have `ComposeAiToolbar` emit the divider + AI `ToolbarButton`s as ITEMS of the EXISTING
      BubbleMenu `&lt;Toolbar&gt;` (pass-through, no nested Toolbar), so the divider gets Toolbar context and one
      flex/gap system governs the whole bar. Acceptable alternative: keep a nested Toolbar but move the divider
      INSIDE it and add `flexWrap: 'wrap'` + a `maxWidth` to `styles.bubbleMenu`. Either way: remove the
      orphaned top-level divider, and drop the redundant `display:flex`/`columnGap` override in `styles.toolbar`
      that fights Fluent's own Toolbar layout. Use semantic tokens (ADR-021), verify dark mode.
    </notes>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project (E2E DoD)">This is a UI-render defect: DoD is a render/DOM assertion (React Testing Library or the project's component test harness) that the popup mounts as a single Toolbar with the divider inside Toolbar context and no overflow — not merely a build-pass. The toolbar must also be shown MOUNTED + REACHABLE in the BubbleMenu.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens only; no hard-coded colors; dark-mode correct.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT change the 5 action ids, dispatch wiring, or the disabled-until-bindingId gating (that is task 048's contract).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No auth/fetch changes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>compose/inline-toolbar, tiptap-bubblemenu, fluent-v9-toolbar</topic>
    <files>
