    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <justification component="No new component — corrects existing Toolbar composition">
    <existing>ComposeAiToolbar + the BubbleMenu Toolbar already exist (task 030).</existing>
    <extension>Refactor the existing composition (fold AI items into the host Toolbar / fix divider context + overflow). No new component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The inline AI affordance — the primary FR-14 surface — renders visibly broken, undermining the whole inline-AI UX the owner just tested.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load the triage note + task 030 + ADR-021. Read `ComposeAiToolbar.tsx:357-363/482-485` and `ComposeEditor.tsx:461-470/848-899` to confirm the composition.</step>
    <step order="1">Refactor so the AI divider + action buttons are children of a SINGLE Toolbar (fold into the host BubbleMenu Toolbar, pass-through), OR move the divider inside the nested Toolbar and add flexWrap+maxWidth to `bubbleMenu`. Remove the orphaned top-level `&lt;ToolbarDivider/&gt;`.</step>
    <step order="2">Drop the redundant `display:flex`/`columnGap` override in `styles.toolbar`; rely on Fluent Toolbar layout. Ensure buttons wrap or the bar caps width; verify dark mode + semantic tokens.</step>
    <step order="3">Add/extend a component render test asserting: one Toolbar in the popup, the divider is within Toolbar context, all 5 AI buttons present, and the bar does not overflow (width-cap or wrap). Confirm the toolbar mounts inside the BubbleMenu (reachable).</step>
    <step order="4">Recompile the shared lib (`@spaarke/ui-components`/compose components) per code-page-deploy cache rules; run the component tests + lint.</step>
    <step order="5">code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5). Update TASK-INDEX + current-task.md.</step>
  </steps>

